    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: pure-Python WHATWG URL Standard implementation (MIT).

Needed by skillspector &gt;= 2.11.0 for bundled-hook URL analysis.

%check runs the real WPT URL conformance suite (1600 cases). The sdist ships
the suite but not its fixtures -- upstream CI downloads them -- so three WPT
JSONs are carried as Source1..3, pinned to the tarball's DEFAULT_WPT_COMMIT and
byte-identical to the declared raw.githubusercontent.com URLs. Without them
pytest does not collect at all. test_wpt_idna.py / test_wpt_toascii.py are
excluded: upstream marks them xfail because python-idna enforces RFC 5891/5892,
stricter than WHATWG's lenient UTS46.

Requires: python-idna is declared by hand -- pythondistdeps does not emit it
despite Requires-Dist: idna&gt;=3.4 in the installed METADATA (rpmlint:
python-missing-require idna).

rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings.</comment>
